passerine<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passerine>
bird <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird> that was formerly classed as a
member of the thrush <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrush_%28bird%29>family
Turdidae <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turdidae>, but is now more generally
considered to be an Old World
flycatcher<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_World_flycatcher>,
Muscicapidae <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muscicapidae>. It belongs to a
group of more terrestrial species, often called
chats<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chat_%28bird%29>
.

